<title>GERMANY: Boehringer Ingelheim says 96 net profit up 20 pct.</title>
<headline>Boehringer Ingelheim says 96 net profit up 20 pct.</headline>
<dateline>FRANKFURT 1997-04-23</dateline>
<text>
<p>Calendar 1996 (in millions of marks unless stated)</p>
<p>    Group net profit			   327     vs 273</p>
<p>    Operating profit			   651     vs 675</p>
<p>    Group sales -				7,085   vs 6,429</p>
<p>sales by region</p>
<p>     sales in Europe			   46 pct  vs 47 pct</p>
<p>     sales N. America and S. America     35 pct  vs 31 pct</p>
<p>     sales in Asia, Australia, Africa    19 pct  vs 22 pct</p>
<p>sales by business area</p>
<p>     human pharmaceuticals		   84 pct  vs 84 pct</p>
<p>     other business areas		    16 pct  vs 16 pct</p>
<p>    Group cash flow			    834     vs 763</p>
<p>    Return on sales			    4.6 pct vs 4.2 pct</p>
<p>    Return on equity			   9.8 pct vs 9.2 pct</p>
<p>    Group equity				 3,631   vs 3,347</p>
<p>    Group investments in fixed assets    676     vs 396</p>
<p>    Research and development		 1,225   vs 1,068</p>
<p>    Personnel costs			    2,255   vs 2,024</p>
<p>Workforce (including workforce</p>
<p>    from joint ventures)		     24,074  vs 23,277</p>
<p>NOTE - Full company name of the privately-owned German pharmaceutical company is Boehringer Ingelheim.</p>
<p>--Frankfurt Newsroom +49 69 756525</p>
</text>
